{
  "Comment": "Cerberus 4.2/4.3 -- full ingest -> transform -> dbt -> serve orchestration (ADR 0009). Each state's own Comment explains its Retry policy's reasoning -- InvokeIngestion deliberately has none (ADR 0005: retrying would regenerate and duplicate unseeded data), RunTransform retries once and RunDbt twice (both are idempotent end to end; see each state's Comment). TimeoutSeconds on every state is the outer safety net against an ECS task hanging past its own internal poll-loop bound (see entrypoint_transform.sh's SPARK_POLL_MAX_ATTEMPTS/REPAIR_POLL_MAX_ATTEMPTS) or a native integration never returning. Execution-level visibility (CloudWatch Logs, X-Ray) is configured on the aws_sfn_state_machine resource itself, not in this definition.",
  "StartAt": "InvokeIngestion",
  "States": {
    "InvokeIngestion": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${ingestion_lambda_arn}"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.ingestion",
      "TimeoutSeconds": 120,
      "Comment": "Deliberately no Retry block (4.3). A retry here re-invokes the Lambda from scratch, re-running its intentionally unseeded generator (payments_lib.py) and appending a different dataset into append-only bronze -- exactly the risk ADR 0005 eliminated by setting the EventBridge Scheduler target's own maximum_retry_attempts to 0. A Step Functions-level retry would reintroduce it one layer up. Genuine failures still route to PipelineFailed via Catch below.",
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "PipelineFailed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "RunTransform"
    },
    "RunTransform": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::ecs:runTask.sync",
      "Parameters": {
        "LaunchType": "FARGATE",
        "Cluster": "${ecs_cluster_arn}",
        "TaskDefinition": "${transform_task_definition_arn}",
        "NetworkConfiguration": {
          "AwsvpcConfiguration": {
            "Subnets": ${subnet_ids_json},
            "SecurityGroups": ["${security_group_id}"],
            "AssignPublicIp": "DISABLED"
          }
        }
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.transform",
      "TimeoutSeconds": 4500,
      "Comment": "TimeoutSeconds 4500 (8.9): above the runner's own 60-minute Spark bound (SPARK_POLL_MAX_ATTEMPTS) plus the ECS task's start and stop. MaxAttempts 1 (8.9; 2 since 4.3): a retry is safe -- entrypoint_transform.sh deletes any prior SparkApplication before resubmitting, and the job's anti-join on (transaction_id, event_type) skips events an earlier attempt already committed to silver (ADR 0017) -- but at 100M an attempt runs about half an hour, so one retry covers a transient failure and a second would mostly repeat a deterministic one.",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "IntervalSeconds": 30,
          "MaxAttempts": 1,
          "BackoffRate": 2.0
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "PipelineFailed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "RunDbt"
    },
    "RunDbt": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::ecs:runTask.sync",
      "Parameters": {
        "LaunchType": "FARGATE",
        "Cluster": "${ecs_cluster_arn}",
        "TaskDefinition": "${dbt_task_definition_arn}",
        "NetworkConfiguration": {
          "AwsvpcConfiguration": {
            "Subnets": ${subnet_ids_json},
            "SecurityGroups": ["${security_group_id}"],
            "AssignPublicIp": "DISABLED"
          }
        }
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.dbt",
      "TimeoutSeconds": 2700,
      "Comment": "MaxAttempts 2 (4.3): dbt's own +materialized: table config (1.9) does a full rebuild every run, same idempotency property RunTransform's comment above describes -- a retry is a clean redo, not a partial/duplicated one.",
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "IntervalSeconds": 30,
          "MaxAttempts": 2,
          "BackoffRate": 2.0
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "PipelineFailed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "RunServingQuery"
    },
    "RunServingQuery": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::athena:startQueryExecution.sync",
      "Parameters": {
        "QueryString": ${demo_query_json},
        "QueryExecutionContext": {
          "Database": "${athena_database}"
        },
        "WorkGroup": "${athena_workgroup}"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.servingQuery",
      "TimeoutSeconds": 300,
      "Retry": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["Athena.AmazonAthenaException"],
          "IntervalSeconds": 15,
          "MaxAttempts": 2,
          "BackoffRate": 2.0
        }
      ],
      "Catch": [
        {
          "ErrorEquals": ["States.ALL"],
          "ResultPath": "$.error",
          "Next": "PipelineFailed"
        }
      ],
      "Next": "PipelineSucceeded"
    },
    "PipelineSucceeded": {
      "Type": "Succeed"
    },
    "PipelineFailed": {
      "Type": "Fail",
      "Error": "CerberusPipelineFailed",
      "Cause": "One or more pipeline steps failed - see the failed state's ResultPath ($.error) in this execution's history for details."
    }
  }
}
